<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Helsingør</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Elsinore</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Helsingør is a town in north-eastern Zealand, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a>, at the narrowest point of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oresund">Øresund</a>, opposite <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/helsingborg">Helsingborg</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a>. From around 1429 until 1857 Danish kings levied the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sound-toll">Sound Toll</a> there on ships passing between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-sea">North Sea</a> and the Baltic. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kronborg">Kronborg Castle</a>, rebuilt in the 1570s and 1580s, guarded the strait and is the setting of Shakespeare's &quot;Hamlet&quot;.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/helsingor.jpg" alt="Helsingør" width="320" height="135" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Karen Rustad · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Helsing%C3%B8r_Elsinore_from_sea_01.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
